    "content": "# 10-Mark Questions & Answers — DBMS Module 2: Relational Algebra & Calculus\n\n---\n\n### Q1. Explain Relational Algebra operations (Fundamental & Derived), Joins (Inner, Outer, Semi, Anti), and Relational Calculus in detail with schema queries.\n\nComprehensive solution covering:\n1. Six Fundamental Relational Algebra Operations (Selection, Projection, Union, Set Difference, Cartesian Product, Rename).\n2. Derived Operations: Intersection, Natural Join, Theta Join, Division operator (÷ for \"for all\" queries).\n3. Left, Right, and Full Outer Joins with step-by-step table examples.\n4. Tuple Relational Calculus (TRC) and Domain Relational Calculus (DRC) with existential (∃) and universal (∀) quantifiers.\n5. Equivalence between SQL SELECT queries and Relational Algebra expressions.\n",
    "html": "<h1>10-Mark Questions &amp; Answers — DBMS Module 2: Relational Algebra &amp; Calculus</h1>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q1. Explain Relational Algebra operations (Fundamental &amp; Derived), Joins (Inner, Outer, Semi, Anti), and Relational Calculus in detail with schema queries.</h3>\n<p>Comprehensive solution covering:<br />\n1. Six Fundamental Relational Algebra Operations (Selection, Projection, Union, Set Difference, Cartesian Product, Rename).<br />\n2. Derived Operations: Intersection, Natural Join, Theta Join, Division operator (÷ for \"for all\" queries).<br />\n3. Left, Right, and Full Outer Joins with step-by-step table examples.<br />\n4. Tuple Relational Calculus (TRC) and Domain Relational Calculus (DRC) with existential (∃) and universal (∀) quantifiers.<br />\n5. Equivalence between SQL SELECT queries and Relational Algebra expressions.</p>",
