    "title": "Module 3: 3-Mark Questions & Answers (Linked Lists)",
    "content": "# 3-Mark Questions & Answers — Data Structures Module 3: Linked Lists\n\n---\n\n### Q1. Explain insertion at beginning, middle, and end in a Singly Linked List.\n\n1. **Insert at Beginning (**O(1)**):** `newNode->next = head; head = newNode;`\n2. **Insert at End (**O(N)**):** Traverse to last node `temp->next == NULL`, then `temp->next = newNode;`\n3. **Insert after Position (**O(N)**):** `newNode->next = temp->next; temp->next = newNode;`\n\n---\n\n### Q2. Explain deletion of a node in a Doubly Linked List.\n\nTo delete node `del`:\n```c\nif (del->prev != NULL) del->prev->next = del->next;\nelse head = del->next;\nif (del->next != NULL) del->next->prev = del->prev;\nfree(del);\n```\n\n---\n\n### Q3. Explain Polynomial Representation using Linked Lists.\n\nEach polynomial term **c × x^e** is represented as a node containing:\n- `coeff` (Coefficient **c**)\n- `expo` (Exponent **e**)\n- `next` (Pointer to next term in descending exponent order)\n",
    "html": "<h1>3-Mark Questions &amp; Answers — Data Structures Module 3: Linked Lists</h1>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q1. Explain insertion at beginning, middle, and end in a Singly Linked List.</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Insert at Beginning (</strong>O(1)<strong>):</strong> <code>newNode-&gt;next = head; head = newNode;</code></li>\n<li><strong>Insert at End (</strong>O(N)<strong>):</strong> Traverse to last node <code>temp-&gt;next == NULL</code>, then <code>temp-&gt;next = newNode;</code></li>\n<li><strong>Insert after Position (</strong>O(N)<strong>):</strong> <code>newNode-&gt;next = temp-&gt;next; temp-&gt;next = newNode;</code></li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q2. Explain deletion of a node in a Doubly Linked List.</h3>\n<p>To delete node <code>del</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-c\">if (del-&gt;prev != NULL) del-&gt;prev-&gt;next = del-&gt;next;\nelse head = del-&gt;next;\nif (del-&gt;next != NULL) del-&gt;next-&gt;prev = del-&gt;prev;\nfree(del);\n</code></pre>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q3. Explain Polynomial Representation using Linked Lists.</h3>\n<p>Each polynomial term <strong>c × x^e</strong> is represented as a node containing:<br />\n- <code>coeff</code> (Coefficient <strong>c</strong>)<br />\n- <code>expo</code> (Exponent <strong>e</strong>)<br />\n- <code>next</code> (Pointer to next term in descending exponent order)</p>",
