    "content": "# 5-Mark Questions & Answers — Data Structures Module 6: Sorting & Searching Techniques\n\n---\n\n### Q1. Explain Bubble Sort, Insertion Sort, and Selection Sort with step-by-step trace and C programs.\n\nDetailed algorithms, code implementations, and complexity analysis (**O(N^2)** average, **O(1)** space).\n\n---\n\n### Q2. Explain Merge Sort and Quick Sort algorithms with Divide-and-Conquer recurrence relations.\n\n- **Merge Sort:** Divide in half, recursively sort, merge halves. **T(N) = 2T(N/2) + O(N) \\implies O(N \\log N)** in all cases.\n- **Quick Sort:** Partition around pivot. **O(N \\log N)** average, **O(N^2)** worst case. In-place sorting.\n\n---\n\n### Q3. Explain Collision Resolution Techniques in Hashing with numerical examples.\n\nDetailed walkthrough of Linear Probing, Quadratic Probing, Double Hashing, and Separate Chaining.\n",
    "html": "<h1>5-Mark Questions &amp; Answers — Data Structures Module 6: Sorting &amp; Searching Techniques</h1>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q1. Explain Bubble Sort, Insertion Sort, and Selection Sort with step-by-step trace and C programs.</h3>\n<p>Detailed algorithms, code implementations, and complexity analysis (<strong>O(N^2)</strong> average, <strong>O(1)</strong> space).</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q2. Explain Merge Sort and Quick Sort algorithms with Divide-and-Conquer recurrence relations.</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Merge Sort:</strong> Divide in half, recursively sort, merge halves. <strong>T(N) = 2T(N/2) + O(N) \\implies O(N \\log N)</strong> in all cases.</li>\n<li><strong>Quick Sort:</strong> Partition around pivot. <strong>O(N \\log N)</strong> average, <strong>O(N^2)</strong> worst case. In-place sorting.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Q3. Explain Collision Resolution Techniques in Hashing with numerical examples.</h3>\n<p>Detailed walkthrough of Linear Probing, Quadratic Probing, Double Hashing, and Separate Chaining.</p>",
